					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-245051#post-850828</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-245051/happy-free-market-log-17643390#post-850828</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 16 Aug 2010 10:20:33 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>SophosBlitz</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>327981</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I just assumed the timestamps were in seconds like the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time">UNIX timestamps</a> except that they were working from some unknown arbitrary calendar origin point that the machine adheres to. It's not a detail that needs to be fussed over for suspension of disbelief.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-245051#post-850692</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-245051/happy-free-market-log-17643390#post-850692</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 16 Aug 2010 05:58:23 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Chaoseed</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>479761</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The timestamps are meant to be seconds. You should be able to roughly estimate an actual time of day for each timestamp…if you really want to get into it. ;)</p> <p>However, the "beginning" timestamp was chosen randomly. I didn't calculate 204 days to mean anything in particular. It would probably make sense if 261 had been moved to the SCP facility 204 days ago…but I left it vague in the story, so it's left up to reader interpretation. :)</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-245051#post-835779</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-245051/happy-free-market-log-17643390#post-835779</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 24 Jul 2010 13:43:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>kendrakirai</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>369686</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Hmmmmmmmm</p> <p>Timestamp of 17643390. If we assume this is seconds, that comes out to 204 days.</p> <p>If we assume minutes, that comes out to 33 and a half years.</p> <p>Of course, it may be something completely arbitrary, or not mean anything at all, but I think minutes is a good estimate of how old it is and how long it's been dispensing nourishment and snacks to people. :) I wonder if it was intentional…</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
